    {
      "id": "workspace-connections-n-start",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Start here",
      "position": {
        "x": 3000,
        "y": 0
      },
      "width": 640,
      "height": 430,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "workspace-connections-declaration",
          "nodeId": "workspace-connections-n-start"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "### Start here\n\n**What this is.** A task graph about how the Twilite workspace draws the connection between two open graphs. Its open questions are what needs an answer.\n\n**If you are helping:** read the notes to the right, then the open questions. Say which questions you can answer and why, and what you would want to see first. Do not change code on the strength of these notes alone: the owner has asked for a second opinion first, and says the model below is easy to get wrong."
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1791502752029,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "workspace-connections-n-terms",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "The words, as the owner uses them",
      "position": {
        "x": 3000,
        "y": 470
      },
      "width": 640,
      "height": 430,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "workspace-connections-declaration",
          "nodeId": "workspace-connections-n-terms"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "### The words, as the owner uses them\n\n- **Graph** — one open file, drawn as a tile in the workspace. It has a border.\n- **Port** — a node inside a graph that an edge ends at: an Import or Export node, a Portal node, the node that holds a link, or the Port a portal opens onto.\n- **Handle** — a port on a node: where that node's edge attaches, on the graph's border. The edge ends at the port but passes through its handle.\n- **Edge** — the line between two graphs. It runs port, handle, handle, port.\n\nThe code uses other words: a handle on the border is an `aperture`, and the point where several edges between the same two graphs gather is a `trunk handle` or `collector`. Read the owner's words as the correct ones."
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1791502752029,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "workspace-connections-n-kinds",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Three kinds, and where each end sits today",
      "position": {
        "x": 3000,
        "y": 940
      },
      "width": 640,
      "height": 430,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "workspace-connections-declaration",
          "nodeId": "workspace-connections-n-kinds"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "### Three kinds, and where each end sits today\n\n| Kind | Connects | Handle at the first end | Handle at the other end |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Bridge** (orange, laddered) | An Export node to the Import node that uses it | Right border for an export, left for an import, by role | The same rule at the other graph. Bridges always run left to right. |\n| **Portal** (purple, laddered) | A Portal node to the graph it opens, and the Port it lands on when it names one | The border nearest the Portal node, on any side | Where a straight line between the two graphs' centres crosses the target's border |\n| **Link** (pale blue, dashed) | A node holding a hyperlink to a whole graph. No port on the target | The border nearest the node that holds the link, on any side | Where the line between the centres crosses the target's border |\n\nThe kinds are different things and stay different, in look and in what they connect."
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1791502752029,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "workspace-connections-n-wrong",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "What looks wrong, and what is not known",
      "position": {
        "x": 3000,
        "y": 1410
      },
      "width": 640,
      "height": 430,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "workspace-connections-declaration",
          "nodeId": "workspace-connections-n-wrong"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "### What looks wrong, and what is not known\n\nBridges follow a fixed rule, so they tidy up well. Portals and links do not: their handles land on any side, and at the far end wherever a diagonal crosses the border. The router then draws from a handle on the top side to a graph to the lower right, so the line leaves and enters in directions that do not face its partner, and crosses other lines. Several lines between the same two graphs are also drawn along the border as thin faded wraps before they reach a shared point.\n\n**Not yet known.** The long diagonal purple lines in the owner's screenshot could not be reproduced: in a test scene portals and bridges both ran at right angles. That scene may have been set to Straight, or arranged by hand. See a live scene first."
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1791502752029,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "workspace-connections-n-code",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Where the code is",
      "position": {
        "x": 3000,
        "y": 1880
      },
      "width": 640,
      "height": 430,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "workspace-connections-declaration",
          "nodeId": "workspace-connections-n-code"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "### Where the code is\n\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/workspaceBridge.js` — where each kind's ends are placed: `deriveWorkspacePortalGeometry`, `deriveWorkspaceLinkGeometry`, `deriveWorkspaceBridgeGeometry`.\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/workspaceEdgeCanvas.js` — turns those ends into edges for the painter, and groups edges between the same two graphs.\n- `components/GraphEditor/components/WorkspaceLayer.js` — draws the wraps and the names on the edges, and takes clicks on a connection.\n- `components/NodeGraph/EdgeLayer.js` — the painter and router, shared with edges inside a graph.\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/workspaceCommands.js` — the bar and menu commands: Connections, Organise, Tidy.\n\nTo see it: open the Templates index and a few of its templates in the workspace, press Organise workspace, then Connections to step through the three styles."
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1791502752029,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    }
